00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.949 align:start position:0%
call of duty infinite Warfare's  multiplayer may not seem that dramatic a  shift from last year's black ops 3 but  there are some important lessons and  tips for those of you jumping in to  consider here are a couple of them it's  essential to master wall running sliding  and thrust jumping as it greatly  improves your ability to traverse the  environment which in turn makes you a  harder target to hit  for instance wall running and thrust  jumping can throw off enemy fire while  sliding can be used to quickly zip into  cover take the time to understand how  each of these actions affect your  mobility as performing them recklessly  is likely to get you killed  always keep an eye on your radar this  may seem like an obvious one but  beginners often forget it even exists  the radar is an incredibly useful tool  that reveals both allies and enemy  locations  infinite Warfare's biggest change is the  new class system combat rigs which are  special classes you can choose they each  offer their own distinct weapon and  abilities with six different rigs to  choose from it's easy to stick to one  you're comfortable with however each  combat rig has their own unique weapons  and abilities that make them fully  capable of racking up a large string of  kills even if you think a combat rig may  not be suitable to your play style it's  best to experiment with each one a  greater understanding of each one makes  you a better player overall as it not  only enhances your knowledge of what  each one can do but how you can counter  the others as you play the various  multiplayer modes you'll start to earn a  currency called keys these can be used  to purchase supply drops which are loop  boxes that net you a set of three random  items which include prototype weapons  combat rig items and personalization  colors supply drops can be purchased in  both multiplayer and zombies but it's  worth noting that the latter devotes one  of the three items you earn to a pack of  zombie mode cards if you don't play  zombies make sure you spend your keys  exclusively in multiplayer as doing  otherwise will only be a waste in the  long run new to infinite warfare is the  addition of mission teams which are  special groups you can join that give  you objectives to complete during a  match accomplishing these objectives  earns you perks combat rig paint jobs  and prototype weapons that are each  unique to your mission team make sure to  complete your team's current objective  unit whenever possible the wards you  unlock are worth your time  unlike past Call of Duty games infinite  warfare lets you lob your grenade with  your left arm allowing you to continue  firing your weapon during the throwing  animation be sure to take advantage of  this as it can be a handy way to cover  yourself while throwing a cooked burn  aid towards a group of baddies prototype  weapons are some of these strongest  weapons in the game  so it's best to get your hands on as  many as possible  similar to loot games like destiny they  come in tiers common rare legendary and  epic you can acquire these weapons by  crafting them with Salvage opening up  supply drops or leveling up your faction  when playing defender pay attention to  the timer depending on the situation and  your placement on the map the timer can  determine the best course of action for  example if the timer is nearly up and  the enemy with the ball is far away try  seeking out the balls next spawn point  instead of pursuing it helps to be  methodical about the flow of the match  as opposed to mindlessly following the  ball wherever it goes don't hesitate to  shamelessly hide when you've got the  ball in defender there's no need to pull  over-the-top maneuvers your sometimes  better just finding a place to hide and  sticking there as the timer goes down if  you can't find a spot stay with your  teammates and keep moving away from the  enemy team and there are some tips to  get you guys started with infinite  Warfare's multiplayer are you enjoying  the game please let us know in the  comments below and have a great day
 

